//? Title: Training Metrics: Counts, Rankings and Aggregation
//? Subtitle: State the class set, tie rule and sample weights before interpreting a score
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A single training score can hide which classes fail, how score ties are handled or how
unequal batches were averaged. We construct small labelled examples whose confusion
counts, ranking comparisons and weighted means can be checked by hand. The native
metrics are evaluated on those fixed inputs; no classifier is fitted or selected. A
separate score-tie example distinguishes argmax accuracy from this library's strictly
higher-score top-k convention.
)
\toc

> The method


A confusion matrix stores truth in rows and predictions in columns. For one class,
precision=TP/(TP+FP), recall=TP/(TP+FN), F1=2TP/(2TP+FP+FN), and
IoU=TP/(TP+FP+FN). Zero-denominator precision/recall/F1 are zero here; IoU is NaN if
that class never occurs in truth or predictions. Accuracy counts all correct observations.
Macro precision/recall/F1 average per-class ratios over the configured class set; macro
IoU ignores undefined class IoUs. Thus adding absent classes can change macro F1.

For binary ranking, ROC AUC has the pairwise interpretation

$$
 \mathrm{AUC}=\frac{\sum_{i:y_i=1}\sum_{j:y_j=0}
 (\mathbf1[s_i>s_j]+\tfrac12\mathbf1[s_i=s_j])}{n_+n_-}.
$$
\alttext(ROC AUC counts positive-negative wins, adding half for equal-score pairs.)

Average precision groups tied score thresholds and sums precision weighted by each recall
increase. It does not use trapezoidal interpolation between precision-recall points.
Neither ranking score fixes a decision threshold, measures probability calibration or
by itself determines utility at a specific operating point. ROC AUC requires both classes;
no-positive average precision is zero in this implementation. Inputs are finite scores
and binary labels in these examples. Averages over batches must respect sample counts.


The concept diagram is generated from the retained local TikZ source. LaTeX with
PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm, is needed only to regenerate it.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/metrics_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/metrics_concept.tikz > build/metrics.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/metrics_concept.svg build/metrics_concept.dvi > build/metrics.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/metrics_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
